  "body": "**Link to problem area**:\r\n\r\n- https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#get_matrixclientv3useruseridaccount_datatype\r\n- https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#put_matrixclientv3useruseridaccount_datatype\r\n- https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#get_matrixclientv3useruseridroomsroomidaccount_datatype\r\n- https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#put_matrixclientv3useruseridroomsroomidaccount_datatype\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\n\r\n- What happens if you try to GET or PUT account data for a different user? Synapse returns 403 with M_FORBIDDEN.\r\n- What happens if you try to GET or PUT account data to a user_id that isn't a matrix id? 403 probably suffices, but 400 might also be appropriate.\r\n- What happens if you try to GET a `type` of account data which isn't stored on the server? Synapse returns 404.\r\n- Synapse also special-cases an attempt to PUT `m.fully_read`:,returning 405 (Method not allowed).\r\n  - https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/e24ff8ebe3d4119d377355402245947f7de61c00/synapse/rest/client/account_data.py#L109-L114\r\n  - Ahh, this is mandated by https://spec.matrix.org/v1.3/client-server-api/#server-behaviour-10\r\n\r\nSynapse implementation is https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/e24ff8ebe3d4119d377355402245947f7de61c00/synapse/rest/client/account_data.py\r\n\r\nMore generally, see #1145 ",
